6. **Increased Patient Satisfaction:** Patients often report improved quality of life and satisfaction from incorporating C.A.T. into their care.

However, it is important to note that not all nurses advocate for C.A.T. and not all therapies are equally proven or safe. Nurses should carefully evaluate the effectiveness and safety of any C.A.T. before integrating it into their patient care.

