1. Small molecule inhibitors: These are small drugs that can bind to and inhibit the activity of oncogene proteins. For example, tyrosine kinase inhibitors (TKIs) can inhibit the activity of oncogenic kinases, such as those encoded by the epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR) or the human epidermal growth factor receptor 3 (HER3) pathways. These inhibitors can be used to treat various types of cancer, such as lung cancer, breast cancer, and colon cancer.

