6. Heavy (e.g., fat, oils)

The distribution of taste buds on the tongue surface is not as strict and localized as the common misconception suggests. Contrary to the common image of color-colored regions for each taste, taste buds are distributed throughout the tongue's surface, including the dorsal surface (top), ventral surface (bottom), and the edges. However, some regions may have higher concentrations of certain types of taste buds. For example, the northern surface may have more bitter taste buds, while the southern surface may have more sweet taste buds. However, this is not a hard boundary, and all taste buds can detect all five basic tastes.
