The debate between Golgi and Cajal was crucial in establishing the neuron doctrine. Golgi and Cajal both used a staining technique called the Gram stain to visualize the structure of the nervous system. Golgi's stain works by staining only a small percentage of cells in a sample, allowing for the observation of individual cells in the context of the surrounding tissue.

