","To calculate the entropy change (\(\Delta S\)) for the reaction, we use the formula:

\[
\Delta S = \sum \Delta S_f(\text{products}) - \sum \Delta S_f(\text{reactants})
\]

For the given reaction:

1. **For the products**:
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{products}} = 2 \times \Delta S_f(\text{PbO}) + 2 \times \Delta S_f(\text{SO}_2]
   \]
   \[
   = 2 \times 66.5 + 2 \times 248.2 = 133.0 + 496.4 = 629.4 \, \text{J/K mol}
   \]

2. **For the reactants**:
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{reactants}} = 2 \times \Delta S_f(\text{PbS}) + 3 \times \Delta S_f(\text{O}_2]
   \]
   \[
   = 2 \times 91.2 + 3 \times 205.1 = 182.4 + 615.3 = 797.7 \, \text{J/K mol}
   \]

3. **Calculate \(\Delta S\)**:
   \[
   \Delta S = \Delta S_{\text{products}} - \Delta S_{\text{reactants}} = 629.4 - 797.7 = -168.3 \, \text{J/K mol}
   \]

Thus, the entropy change for the reaction is \(\boxed{-168.3 \, \text{J/K mol}}\).
