","1. **Calculate the area of the courtyard:**  
   \[
   \text{Area} = \text{Length} \times \text{Width} = 50 \text{ m} \times 16.5 \text{ m} = 825 \text{ m}^2
   \]

2. **Calculate the area of one paving stone:**  
   \[
   \text{Area of one stone} = \text{Length} \times \text{Width} = 2.5 \text{ m} \times \text{Width}
   \]

3. **Set up the equation to find the width of the paving stone:**  
   \[
   \text{Number of stones} \times \text{Area of one stone} = \text{Area of courtyard}
   \]  
   \[
   165 \times (2.5 \text{ m} \times \text{Width}) = 825 \text{ m}^2
   \]

4. **Solve for the width:**  
   \[
   412.5 \text{ m} \times \text{Width} = 825 \text{ m}^2
   \]  
   \[
   \text{Width} = \frac{825}{412.5} = 2 \text{ m}
   \]

   Therefore, the width of each paving stone is \(\boxed{2 \text{ m}}\).
