   \[
   \binom{15}{6} = \frac{15!}{6! \times 9!} = 1260
   \]
   This accounts for all possible groups of 6 people, regardless of their positions.

2. **Fixed Positions**: Since the order of the positions is fixed (center, P.F., S.F., SF, P.G., SG), we don't need to consider permutations (order of selection). The number of ways to choose the starting lineup is the same as the number of ways to choose 6 people out of 15.

