2. **Convert the distance to meters:**
   - \(102,\!000 \text{ cm} = 102 \text{ m}\).

3. **Calculate Lucy's time to walk the same distance:**
   - Lucy walks at 90 steps/minute, so the time is:
     \[
     \frac{102 \text{ m}}{90 \text{ steps/min}} = \frac{102 \text{ m}}{90 \text{ steps/min}} \times \frac{1 \text{ step}}{55 \text{ cm}} \times \frac{100 \text{ cm}}{1 \text{ m}} = \frac{102 \times 100}{90 \times 55} \text{ min}
     \]
