   \[
   \text{Total time} = 10:30 \text{ AM} - 8:00 \text{ AM} = 2 \text{ hours and 30 minutes} = 150 \text{ minutes}.
   \]

2. **Determine the duration of one exam**: As the exams are equally time-consuming and two exams took a total of 150 minutes, the duration of one exam is:
   \[
   \text{Duration of one exam} = \frac{150 \text{ minutes}}{2} = 75 \text{ minutes}.
   \]

