\[
f_i(\mathbf{r}, \mathbf{p}) = \frac{1}{e^{(\epsilon_i - \tilde{\mu}_i)/kT}}
\]

where \(\epsilon_i\) is the energy of the species \(i\), \(\tilde{\mu}_i\) is the relativistic chemical potential, \(k\) is the Boltzmann constant, and \(T\) is the temperature.

