<start_of_turn>model
","(a) The proton is subject to a force \(F = qE\), where \(q = 1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C}\) and \(E = 500 \, \text{N/C}\).  
\[
F = (1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C})(500 \, \text{N/C}) = 8.00 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}
\]
Using Newton's second law, \(F = ma\), the acceleration is:
\[
a = \frac{F}{m} = \frac{8.00 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} = 4.76 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2
\]
(b) The proton starts from rest (\(u = 0\)), so the kinematic equation \(v^2 = u^2 + 2as\) applies.  Solving for time \(t\):
\[
t = \frac{v - u}{a} = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s} - 0}{4.76 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2} = 6.35 \times 10^{-6} \, \text{s}
\]
Thus, the time required is \(\boxed{6.35 \times 10^{-6} \, \text{s}}\).
