   \[
   \mathbf{\sigma}'_{ij} = L_{ik} L_{jl} \mathbf{\sigma}_{kl}
   \]
   This shows that the components of \( \mathbf{\sigma} \) transform as a second-order tensor.

3. **Conclusion:**
   The electrical conductivity tensor \( \mathbf{\sigma}_{ij} \) transforms as a second-order tensor because its components obey the transformation law \( \mathbf{\sigma}'_{ij} = L_{ik} L_{jl} \mathbf{\sigma}_{kl} \). This ensures that the constitutive relation \( \mathbf{j} = \mathbf{\sigma} \mathbf{E} \) holds in any coordinate system. 

